{{Protection}}{{Title Icon}}
Trophies are a measure of the player's progression with each Brawler, and total game progression. They are awarded or deducted based on the results of a match. Each [[Brawler]] has its own Trophy count, and this determines the Brawler's Tier. All of a player's Brawlers' individual Trophies combine to give them their total Trophy count. As a Brawler reaches higher Tiers, they begin to gain fewer and lose more Trophies in each match. Trophies can only be gained or lost in Trophy game modes.

==Obtaining==
Trophies are obtained by playing Trophy [[Events]]. If a player's team wins in 3v3 and 5v5 modes, or they outlast enough opponents/teams in [[Showdown]], they receive Trophies. They lose Trophies, however, if their team loses or they are defeated early playing Showdown.

When players earn or lose Trophies, they are awarded to or taken away from the Brawler used during that match. The number of Trophies lost or earned from a match changes based on a Brawler's individual Trophy count.

Obtaining Trophies becomes increasingly harder as more Trophies are accumulated. At low Trophy ranges, a Brawler receives more Trophies for a victory than they lose in a defeat. As the Brawler reaches higher Trophies, more Trophies are deducted for losing. This effect increases in severity until it causes the Brawler to lose more Trophies than they can gain with each match, creating a gradual barrier to Trophy accumulation.

After Prestige 2 (2000 Trophies), Bot Matches are disabled, Trophies are not gained from a Win Streak, the Underdog bonus is disabled, and player names are hidden if the average Trophies of everyone in the match is more than 2000. Additionally, the matchmaking blacklisting time gets increased, which serves as a protection against win-traders. All of these factors make it much harder to make progress when pushing for these high ranks.

