==Tips==
*It is important to learn which Brawlers excel at each mode, as oftentimes the results of a match might be due to which Brawlers each team has. The right Brawler in the right event might result in a massive Trophy gain after a few matches, while a Brawler on the weaker side might result in a losing streak even when played well.
*When struggling with a new Brawler, camping within bushes in a Showdown match will rack up Trophies quickly. Avoid all conflict and wait until there are a few Brawlers remaining. The main downside of this method is that it can be slow and less entertaining than continuously fighting. Note that this strategy will not work as well with low- or delayed-damage Brawlers, like throwers and healers, since they are likely to lose an encounter with another Brawler that comes into the same bush.
*When trying to increase total Trophy count, remember it is much easier to gain Trophies with lower Trophy Brawlers.
*Playing with a team can increase the chances of winning matches, as this allows players to plan out and try out multiple strategies with friends/clubmates.

