===Removed Features===
{|class="article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed"
!Season Trophies
|-
|[[File:Season Trophy.png|x100px|right]]
Season Trophies were added in the [[Version History#Patch Notes: Angels vs Demons 29/10/24|October 2024 update]] and removed in the [[Version History/2026#Release Notes February 2026|Feburary 2026 update]]. They were gained instead of normal Trophies after 1000 for Brawlers and contributed to the [[Trophy Box]]. If a Brawler lost Season Trophies, they were not removed from the Trophy Box progress. If a Brawler lost a game with more than 1000 Trophies, they couldn't drop below 1000 Trophies, unless a game was lost at 1000 Trophies.

Trophy seasons coincided with [[Brawl Pass]] seasons, and, at the end of every season, each player's Brawlers would lose their Season Trophies. In addition, players received a bigger Trophy Box the more Season Trophies they had at the end of a season, so more Trophies resulted in better rewards.
|}
{|class="article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed"
!Prestige
|-
|[[File:Prestige.png|x100px|right]]
Prestige was added in the [[Version History#Patch Notes: Angels vs Demons 29/10/24|October 2024 update]] and removed in the [[Version History/2026#Release Notes February 2026|Feburary 2026 update]]. It was obtained at the end of a season for each Brawler a player had in the top 200 global leaderboard. The Prestige for each individual Brawler prior to its removal can be viewed in the Leaderboards under the "Legacy" tab and the total Prestige is shown under "Previous Stats" in a player's profile.
|}

